# Operator scratchpads / sibling checkouts (NOT part of yen-gov).
# These are local-only inspection scripts and unrelated project checkouts
# that sit alongside yen-gov but never get committed. If you want one of
# the inspect_*.py scripts to become a real tool, move it under
# tools/<purpose>/ with a proper docstring and remove its line below.
ai-engineering-coach/
backend/inspect_topn.py
tools/inspect_elections_corpus.py
tools/inspect_state_event_matrix.py
datasets/ephemeral/pre-regen-parquet-snapshot/

# Parity oracle (PR-W1c): cached IndiaVotes HTML snapshots + the throwaway
# operator venv the README tells operators to spin up. NEVER committed.
datasets/ephemeral/indiavotes-snapshots/
.venv-parity/

# PR-9 (Wikidata party-leadership snapshots): the SPARQL JSON response is
# operator-fetched via `python -m yen_gov.sources.wikidata.party_leadership
# snapshot`. The committed artefacts are datasets/data/entities/parties_leadership.csv
# (the canonical store) + datasets/_ops/wikidata-party-qids.json (the
# Wikipedia->Q-id resolution cache); the daily snapshot JSON itself is
# throwaway local state.
datasets/ephemeral/wikidata-party-leadership-*.json


# TopoJSON converter idempotency sidecars (local-only; cross-worktree re-emit is cheap and deterministic).
*.topojson.meta.json
*.tmp_*
.tmp_*
